# The paths below leave every `git archive` of this repository, and so leave
# `dist`, the branch the plugin directory reads, whose tree at each release
# is the archive of the release's tag. They are this repository's own
# development: its suites, its records, what only a contributor's session
# reads, and `.github/`, which leaves whole by one line. It holds this
# repository's workflows, the release automation they run and GitHub's
# templates, and no file `dist` holds loads one of them. The workflows
# also have to leave, because GitHub refuses a push made with a workflow's
# own token that creates or changes a file under `.github/workflows/`, so a
# `dist` commit holding them would never be pushed. A module a shipped file
# loads stands under a directory `dist` holds. This file lists what leaves
# and not what stays, because a path forgotten here reaches `dist` and costs
# size or a directory finding, where a path forgotten in a list of what
# stays would be missing from every copy the directory serves with nothing
# in this repository to show it. A pull request that adds a path only
# development reads adds its line here.
#
# The last block leaves for the directory's sake alone. The directory
# refuses a file outside the types it accepts from an organization that is
# not Verified, and nothing installed reads these: the drawings' vector and
# terminal sources under `assets/seals/`, from which the shipped PNGs are
# drawn, the linter's config, and this file, which the archive reads at the
# tag and `dist` never needs.
/tests/ export-ignore
/evals/ export-ignore
/seal/ export-ignore
/CLAUDE.md export-ignore
/.github/ export-ignore
/assets/seals/*.svg export-ignore
/assets/seals/*.ans export-ignore
/ruff.toml export-ignore
/.gitattributes export-ignore
